#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:12
msgid "Coffee Help"
msgstr "咖啡模组帮助"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:24
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Finding the correct coffee route can be quite tricky! First of all, please "
"read the coffee section of the expansion rules. <br /> Make sure you fully "
"understand the example and the reasons why each route was chosen. <br /> The "
"Ketchup Expansion rules are available <a "
"href=\"%(fcm_ketchup_rules_url)s\">here</a>."
msgstr "找到正确的咖啡路线可能相当棘手！首先请阅读扩展规则的咖啡部分。<br /> 请确保完全理解示例以及选择每条路线的原因。<br /> "
"番茄酱扩展规则见 <a href=\"%(fcm_ketchup_rules_url)s\">此处</a>。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:35
msgid "What goes into finding a valid coffee route?"
msgstr "如何找到有效的咖啡路线？"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:38
msgid ""
"Remember the following: <br /> <li>Players actually need to have coffee in "
"stock for a sale to be considered</li> <li> A house can travel along any "
"route to get to the winning restaurant, as long as the <b>tile distance</b> "
"does not go above the minimum required to get to the restaurant </li> <li> "
"If the route splits, the house will choose the route that sells the most "
"coffee <ul> <li> For example, if the route splits and one route sells a "
"coffee to players A and B, and the other route sells a coffee to player C "
"only, then the path selling only to player C will be <b>completely ignored</"
"b> because there is an alternative valid route that sells more coffee, and "
"the house will take the route that sells the most possible coffee </li> </"
"ul> </li> <li> If the route splits and each possible split would sell the "
"<b>same</b> amount of coffee, then <b>no</b> coffee is sold along this split "
"part of the route <ul> <li> This applies even if each path would sell the "
"same amount of coffee to the same player. Why? Because that's what the "
"designer has said! You can think of it as the house arguing about <i>which</"
"i> of the coffee selling places is better, to the point where they end up "
"skipping all of them, even if they belong to the same chain. </li> </li> "
"<li> Consider the example above with one path selling to players A and B, "
"and the other path only to player C. What would happen if player B had no "
"coffee? You would now be in the situation where one route woulf sell to "
"player A and the other route to player C. Both routes would now sell the "
"same amount of coffe, and so now <b>both</b> routes are skipped. </li>"
msgstr ""
"请记住以下几点：<br /> <li>玩家必须实际有咖啡库存才计销售</li> <li> 房屋可走"
"任意路线到达获胜餐厅，只要<b>板块距离</b>不超过到达餐厅的最低要求 </li> <li> "
"若路线分岔，房屋会选择卖出最多咖啡的路线 <ul> <li> 例如一条路线向玩家 A 和 B "
"各卖一杯，另一条只向 C 卖一杯，则只向 C 卖的路径会被<b>完全忽略</b>，因为存在"
"卖出更多咖啡的有效替代路线，房屋会走卖出最多的路线 </li> </ul> </li> <li> 若"
"分岔后各可能分岔卖出的咖啡<b>相同</b>，则该分岔段<b>不</b>卖任何咖啡 <ul> "
"<li> 即使各路径向同一玩家卖出相同数量也适用。为何？设计师就是这么说的！可以理"
"解为房屋在争论<i>哪个</i>卖咖啡的地方更好，结果全部跳过，即使属于同一连锁。 "
"</li> </li> <li> 考虑上面一条路径卖给 A 和 B、另一条只卖给 C 的例子。若玩家 "
"B 没有咖啡会怎样？现在一条卖给 A、另一条卖给 C，两边卖出相同，因此<b>两条</b>"
"都被跳过。 </li>"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:78
msgid ""
"When I click \"More Information\" in the coffee section in \"History\", what "
"exactly are the non-road highlights?"
msgstr ""
"当我在“历史记录”中的咖啡部分点击“更多信息”时，非路线上的高亮部分指什么？"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:81
msgid ""
"Restaurants / coffee shops that are highlighted indicate where coffee was "
"actually sold along the route taken by this house. <br /> Note that the "
"squares highlighted correspond to where the restaurants / coffee shops were "
"on this turn, not where they are now if they were moved later. <br /> So if "
"a non-road square has a highlight but does not contain a restaurant or "
"coffee shop, then it must have been moved after this turn."
msgstr ""
"高亮的餐厅/咖啡店表示本房屋路线上实际售出咖啡的位置。<br /> 注意高亮方格对应"
"的是本回合餐厅/咖啡店的位置，而非其后来被移动后的位置。<br /> 因此若非道路方"
"格有高亮却不含餐厅或咖啡店，则它一定是在本回合之后被移动的。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:96
msgid ""
"When I click \"More Information\" in the coffee section in \"History\", what "
"exactly are the road highlights?"
msgstr ""
"当我在“历史记录”中的“咖啡”部分点击“更多信息”时，路线上的高亮区域具体是指什"
"么？"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:99
msgid ""
"If there is only one valid coffee route from the house to the restaurant, it "
"will be shown. <br /> If there are multiple valid routes, the road squares "
"common to all valid coffee routes will be shown. <br /> This should help you "
"to work out how the sales occurred. Remember distance is only measured in "
"map tiles, not road squares. So if the house could travel one tile right and "
"then one tile down, OR one tile down and then one tile right, AND both "
"choices would sell the same amount of coffee (which would make both valid "
"choices), then none of this section will be highlighted. If however only one "
"of those routes sold coffee, then as both are the same distance, and the "
"house will always choose the route that sells the most coffee, then both the "
"route and the location where the coffee sale occurred should have a "
"highlight. <br /> A route will go all round a tile, if possible, as long as "
"it stays on the same tile and does not make a U-turn. For example, if the "
"route includes the triple lemonade tile from the expansion, or the tile with "
"house 5 on it, then the route will always include all road squares on these "
"tiles"
msgstr ""
"若从房屋到餐厅只有一条有效咖啡路线，将显示该路线。<br /> 若有多条有效路线，将"
"显示所有有效路线共有的道路方格。<br /> 这应有助于你弄清销售如何发生。注意距离"
"只按地图板块计，不按道路方格计。因此若房屋可先右移一板块再下移一板块，或先下"
"移再右移，且两种选择卖出的咖啡相同（两者均有效），则本部分不会高亮。若只有一"
"条路线卖了咖啡，由于距离相同且房屋总会选择卖出最多咖啡的路线，则该路线与销售"
"地点都应高亮。<br /> 可能的话，路线会绕板块一整圈，只要停留在同一板块且不掉"
"头。例如若路线包含扩展中的三倍柠檬水板块，或有 5 号房屋的板块，则总是包含这些"
"板块上的所有道路方格"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:122
msgid ""
"Please consider the following examples to understand better how Coffee "
"Selling works"
msgstr "请考虑以下示例以更好地了解售卖咖啡的正确方式"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:124
msgid ""
"In the following examples, the building with the lemonade makes a sale. "
"Assume all players have 6 coffees. <br /> Xango Blues (green colour) makes "
"the sale, without a drive-thru. Can you work out which locations sell "
"coffee? <br /> In the answers, the locations that sell are circled in green, "
"and the locations that don't sell in red. <br /> Common road squares show "
"the green highlight, and blue lines indicate where there is more than one "
"possible path."
msgstr ""
"在以下示例中，有柠檬水的建筑完成销售。假设所有玩家都有 6 杯咖啡。<br /> "
"Xango Blues（绿色）完成销售，且无得来速。你能算出哪些位置卖了咖啡吗？<br /> "
"答案中，售出位置用绿色圈出，未售出用红色圈出。<br /> 共同道路方格显示绿色高"
"亮，蓝线表示存在多条可能路径。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:135
msgid "Example 1"
msgstr "例1"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:164
msgid "Answer 1"
msgstr "回答1"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:166
msgid ""
"One coffee is sold to Gluttony and one to Xango. The house can travel all "
"the way around the triple lemonade square. It can travel on squares it has "
"already used, as long as it is not making a U-turn. <b>Coffee selling "
"locations don't have to be on the same tile as the route, they just have to "
"be adjacent to the road.</b> House 10 could come out of the house from the "
"bottom left square or top right square, so this part of the route counts as "
"\"undecided\", and no coffee sales would occur along here."
msgstr ""
"Gluttony 和 Xango 各卖了一杯咖啡。顾客可以绕着3个柠檬水广场一直行走。只要不掉"
"头，他们可以在已经走过的方格上行走。<b>卖咖啡的地点不一定在路径所在的相同板块"
"上，它们只需要在道路相邻的位置。</b> 10号房子里的顾客可以从左下方或右上方的方"
"格出门，因此这部分路线被视为“未决定的”，不会出售任何咖啡。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:176
msgid "Example 2"
msgstr "例2"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:205
msgid "Answer 2"
msgstr "回答2"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:207
msgid ""
"Santa Maria sells 2 coffees. House 12 will use any route that doesn't "
"increase tile distance. So they come out onto the road square next to the "
"overpass and sell to Santa Maria. The red circled coffee shops are on "
"mutually exclusive valid routes, each of which would sell one coffee. So "
"both of these coffee shops will be skipped. Note that <b>although there is "
"no green highlighted road directly adjacent to the Santa Maria coffee shop "
"in this section, BOTH (all) valid coffee routes must pass adjacent to it, no "
"matter which route is taken, and so one sale will always occur here as well."
"</b>"
msgstr ""
"Santa Maria 咖啡厅售卖了2杯咖啡。12号房子里的顾客将使用任何不增加板块距离的路"
"线。因此，他们从高架桥旁的道路方块出来，并卖给了 Santa Maria。红圈标出的咖啡"
"店在互斥的有效路径上，每条路径都会卖出一杯咖啡。因此，这两家咖啡店都将被跳"
"过。<b>请注意，尽管没有绿色高亮路径直接毗邻 Santa Maria 咖啡店，但无论采用哪"
"条路线，所有有效咖啡路线都必须经过其相邻的道路，因此在此处始终会发生一次咖啡"
"销售</b>"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:220
msgid "Example 3"
msgstr "例3"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:249
msgid "Answer 3"
msgstr "回答3"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:251
msgid ""
"One coffee is sold by Santa Maria from the middle right tile. This one is a "
"bit more complicated! Remember that the \"winning distance\" for the "
"lemonade sale is 4. So you can never cross more than 4 tile boundaries. "
"Whichever routes you pick at the start, there are essentially the higher "
"route and lower route. The higher route would sell to Santa Maria twice and "
"the lower route to Xango twice. So all of these sales are skipped. "
"Interestingly, there are no road tiles highlighted anywhere near the green "
"circled Santa Maria, but <b>every</b> valid route does pass by it. Remember "
"that a valid route must try to sell as much coffee as possible. So for the "
"house to exit the centre tile to the bottom, it must first go all the way "
"around the tile, passing by the Santa Maria coffee shop, before exiting to "
"the bottom. If the house instead moves onto the right (onto the triple "
"lemonade tile), then it will travel around the entire tile before exiting to "
"the bottom, thus also passing this Santa Maria coffee shop. The same will "
"happen if the house travels along the top and then down onto the triple "
"lemonade tile. So no matter which valid route the house chooses, it will "
"<b>always</b> pass by one Santa Maria coffee shop, but never more than 2 of "
"the other 3 shops, and so these are all skipped. <br /> <br /> Note that "
"there are technically a lot more valid routes than are shown with the blue "
"lines; for example you can exit the apartment tile down onto the central "
"tile from any of the 5 bottom road squares. But in all cases, the outcome is "
"the same."
msgstr ""
"Santa Maria 从右边中间板块卖出一杯咖啡。这个例子更复杂！记住柠檬水销售的“获胜"
"距离”是 4，因此永远不能跨越超过 4 个板块边界。无论一开始选哪些路线，本质上只"
"有上方路线和下方路线。上方路线会向 Santa Maria 卖两次，下方路线向 Xango 卖两"
"次，因此所有这些销售都被跳过。有趣的是，绿色圈出的 Santa Maria 附近没有高亮道"
"路板块，但<b>每条</b>有效路线都经过它。记住有效路线必须尽可能多卖咖啡。因此房"
"屋要从中心板块下方出去，必须先绕板块一整圈经过 Santa Maria 咖啡店再向下。若房"
"屋改向右（进入三倍柠檬水板块），也会绕完整板块后再向下，同样经过这家 Santa "
"Maria。若房屋沿顶部再下到三倍柠檬水板块也是如此。所以无论选择哪条有效路线，都"
"会<b>始终</b>经过一家 Santa Maria 咖啡店，但绝不会经过其他三家中的两家以上，"
"因此这些全被跳过。<br /> <br /> 注意实际上有效路线比蓝线显示的多得多；例如可"
"从底部 5 个道路方格任一处从公寓板块下到中心板块。但所有情况下结果相同。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:275
msgid "Example 4"
msgstr "例4"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:304
msgid "Answer 4"
msgstr "回答4"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:306
msgid ""
"Siap Faji will sell one coffee. Although both blue routes would each sell "
"one coffee to Siap Faji, both locations are skipped, as per the designer's "
"ruling. Think of it as the house arguing about which of the locations is "
"best (even though they belong to the same chain!) and so both locations are "
"skipped. Note that if you replaced the green beer location opposite Xango "
"with a coffee shop, then all routes would now have to pass by this location "
"in order to be a valid route (because it wouldn't increase the tile "
"distance), and so that location would also sell one coffee."
msgstr ""
"Siap Faji 将会卖出一杯咖啡。尽管两条蓝色线路都会分别向 Siap Faji 售出一杯咖"
"啡，但两个咖啡店都被跳过了，根据设计师的规定。可以想象成顾客正在争论哪个咖啡"
"店更好（尽管它们属于同一家连锁店！），因此这两个咖啡店都被跳过了。请注意，如"
"果您用一家咖啡店取代 Xango 对面的啤酒采购点，则为了成为有效的路线，所有路线现"
"在都必须经过这个位置（因为它不会增加板块距离），因此该位置也会售出一杯咖啡。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:314
msgid "I disagree with something on this page?"
msgstr "我不同意此页面上的某些内容？"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\coffeeHelp.html:316
msgid ""
"Coffee is complicated! I had to rewrite the algorithm several times as my "
"understanding of the finer points of the rules changed as I went through "
"development. Any things I wasn't certain of I found clarifications from the "
"game designer on Board Game Geek. I have had a big input from my playtester "
"as well, ensuring that the rules are strictly followed and any ambiguities "
"from the rulebook follow the designer's rulings on BGG. <br /> <br /> If you "
"are unsure, I would strongly urge you to ask in the Board Game Geek forums "
"about it, and if the answer is different to something on this page, please "
"contact me."
msgstr ""
"咖啡很复杂！开发过程中随着我对规则细节理解的变化，我不得不多次重写算法。任何"
"不确定之处，我都在 Board Game Geek 向游戏设计师求证。我的测试员也提供了很大帮"
"助，确保严格遵循规则，规则书中的歧义以 BGG 设计师裁定为准。<br /> <br /> 若不"
"确定，强烈建议你在 Board Game Geek 论坛提问；若答案与本页不同，请联系我。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:12
msgid "Fan Expansions Help"
msgstr "玩家扩展帮助"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:19
msgid ""
"These modules are fan-made expansions. They are not official Splotter "
"Spellen content. <br /> Games with these modules are therefore excluded from "
"the stats. <br /> Fan modules can be enabled in the options when creating a "
"new FCM game."
msgstr ""
"这些模组为玩家自制扩展，并非 Splotter Spellen 官方内容。使用这些模组的游戏不"
"计入统计数据。玩家自制模组可在创建新 FCM 游戏时的选项中开启。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:27
msgid "Fried Chicken"
msgstr "炸鸡"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:41
msgid ""
"Fried chicken is a new food born from unhappy customers. When regular demand "
"goes unserved, frustrated residents start craving fried chicken - and if "
"nobody delivers, they eventually move out of the neighbourhood. Selling the "
"very first fried chicken grants a lucrative but risky monopoly."
msgstr ""
"炸鸡是一种由失望顾客催生的新食物。当普通需求得不到满足时，烦躁的居民开始渴望"
"炸鸡——如果始终无人供应，他们最终会搬离社区。卖出第一份炸鸡将获得一份利润丰厚"
"但风险不小的垄断权。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:49
msgid ""
"Flipping: At Dinnertime, if none of a house's regular demand can be served "
"(every restaurant is too far away, sold out, or too expensive), each "
"unserved regular demand token flips into ownerless demand for Fried Chicken."
msgstr ""
"翻面：晚餐结算时，若一栋房子的需求无法被满足，则每个未被满足的需求标记都会翻"
"面为炸鸡需求。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:54
msgid ""
"Moving out: If flipped Fried Chicken demand is still unserved at its second "
"Dinnertime, the residents move out. All demand is removed, a SOLD sign is "
"placed on the house, and it will not accept any marketing for the rest of "
"the game."
msgstr ""
"搬家：若翻面产生的炸鸡需求在第二次晚餐结算时仍未被满足，居民将搬走（认为城镇"
"没有好吃的食物，太过失望而离开）。所有需求被移除，房子上放置一块 SOLD（已售）"
"牌，且本局游戏不再接受任何营销。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:59
msgid ""
"Origin of demand: Fried Chicken demand is normally only created by flipping "
"- marketing employees cannot create it. Fried Chicken is otherwise a normal "
"food item: it is sold at your normal price, matched by nearest and cheapest "
"as usual, and may be stored in the fridge."
msgstr ""
"需求来源：炸鸡需求通常只能由翻面产生——营销员工无法创造炸鸡需求。除此之外，炸"
"鸡是一种正常食物：按你的正常价格出售，按“最近+最便宜”规则匹配，也可以放进冰"
"箱。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:64
msgid ""
"Milestone \"First fried chicken sold\": The first player to sell Fried "
"Chicken gains this Milestone, which grants two permanent perks: 1) the "
"exclusive right to market Fried Chicken (no other player may ever add it to "
"a campaign), and 2) a brand premium of +$5 for every Fried Chicken sold. The "
"premium applies from the sale after the Milestone is earned, so the "
"milestone-earning sale itself does not get the bonus."
msgstr ""
"里程碑「首个卖出炸鸡」：第一个卖出炸鸡的玩家获得该里程碑，包含两项永久特权："
"1) 炸鸡独家营销权（在营销活动中加入炸鸡）；2) 品牌溢价：每卖出一份炸鸡 +$5。"
"溢价从获得里程碑之后的销售开始生效，触发里程碑的这次销售本身不享受加成。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:69
msgid ""
"Strict liability: Fried Chicken marketed by the Milestone player has only "
"one life. If any marketed Fried Chicken is unserved at Dinnertime, that "
"house moves out at the very next Dinnertime settlement - before any matching "
"takes place and with no flip as a buffer. Regular demand gets two lives "
"(original demand, then flip); marketed Fried Chicken gets just one."
msgstr ""
"严格责任：由里程碑玩家营销的炸鸡只有一条命。若晚餐结算时有任何被营销的炸鸡未"
"被满足，该房子将在下一次晚餐结算时直接搬走。普通需求有两条命（原始需求 + 翻"
"面）；被营销的炸鸡只有一条。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:74
msgid ""
"Employees: Fried Chicken is produced by the Fried Chicken Cook (3 per turn, "
"trained from a Kitchen Trainee; there are 6 in the game) and the Fried "
"Chicken Chef (8 per turn, trained from a Fried Chicken Cook; a 1x employee). "
"A Kitchen Trainee cannot produce Fried Chicken directly. Salaries and "
"training follow the standard employee tiers. When the Fry Chefs module is in "
"use, a Fried Chicken Cook may also be trained into a Fry Chef."
msgstr ""
"员工：炸鸡由炸鸡厨师（每轮制作 3 份，由厨房学徒培训而来；全场共 6 张）和炸鸡"
"主厨（每轮制作 8 份，由炸鸡厨师培训而来；1x 员工）制作。厨房学徒不能直接制作"
"炸鸡。工资和培训遵循标准员工层级。启用炸薯条主厨模组时，炸鸡厨师也可以升级为"
"炸薯条主厨。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:79
msgid ""
"Rural exemption: The Rural Marketing Area never flips and never moves out."
msgstr "乡村豁免：乡村营销区不在城镇之内，所以需求不会翻面，也永远不会搬走。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:88
msgid "Stadium"
msgstr "体育场"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:102
msgid ""
"The Stadium is a giant building spanning two map tiles. On game day the "
"whole city turns into one huge customer: a big crowd with a big appetite for "
"exactly one food. Games are held every 3 turns and announced well in advance "
"- stocking up and pricing become a battle for a winner-takes-all jackpot. "
"Recommended for games with 3 or more players."
msgstr ""
"体育场是一座横跨两个地图板块的巨型建筑。比赛日当天，整座城市会变成一个巨大的"
"顾客：一大群恰好只对一种食物胃口极佳的观众。比赛每 3 回合举办一次，并会提前很"
"久公布——囤货和定价将变成一场争夺赢家通吃头奖的较量。推荐 3 人及以上对局使用。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:110
msgid ""
"The building: When this module is enabled, the Stadium replaces two adjacent "
"map tiles at game start, at a random position and orientation, and stays "
"fixed for the whole game. It is all stadium and surrounding road - no "
"building lots and no houses, so it produces no regular demand. Its value is "
"the road network and game day."
msgstr ""
"建筑：启用本模组后，体育场会在开局时替换两个相邻的地图板块，位置和朝向随机，"
"且整局游戏固定不变。板块上全是体育场及其周边道路——没有建筑地块，也没有房屋，"
"因此不会产生普通需求。它的价值在于道路网络和比赛日。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:115
msgid ""
"Schedule: Games are played on turns 5, 8, 11, ... - every 3 turns, starting "
"with turn 5."
msgstr "日程：比赛在第 5、8、11……回合举行——每 3 回合一次，从第 5 回合开始。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:120
msgid ""
"The announcement: At the end of a turn, 2 turns before each game, an "
"announcement reveals which single food the crowd wants. The food is always "
"mass-market: pizza or burgers, plus noodles, dumplings or fried chicken if "
"that module is enabled in the same game - never sushi, never drinks or "
"kimchi."
msgstr ""
"公告：每场比赛前 2 回合的回合结束时，会发布公告揭示观众想要的那一种食物。食物"
"始终属于大众品类：披萨或汉堡；若同一局游戏启用了相应模组，还可能是面条、饺子"
"或炸鸡——绝不会是寿司，也绝不会是饮料或泡菜。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:125
msgid ""
"Crowd size: 6 units at the first game, 12 at the second, and 16 from the "
"third game onward."
msgstr "观众规模：第一场比赛 6 份，第二场 12 份，第三场及以后为 16 份。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:130
msgid ""
"Dinnertime on game day: The Stadium (house number 0.1) eats before every "
"house. Standard matching rules apply: among the restaurants that have the "
"full amount in stock, the nearest one wins, ties broken by cheapest price. "
"The winner sells all units in a single sale."
msgstr ""
"比赛日的晚餐结算：体育场（0.1 号房屋）先于所有房屋用餐。适用标准匹配规则：在"
"备有全部所需数量的餐厅中，距离最近者获胜，并列时价格最低者优先。获胜餐厅通过"
"一笔销售卖出全部份数。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:135
msgid ""
"One-day event: If no restaurant can supply the full amount, the demand "
"disappears at Dinnertime - the game is not postponed."
msgstr ""
"单日赛事：若没有餐厅能供应全部数量，需求将在晚餐结算时消失——比赛不会延期。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:140
msgid ""
"Isolation: Stadium demand never flips into Fried Chicken and never moves "
"out. It cannot be targeted by marketing campaigns, and substitution effects "
"(noodle or sushi replacements, kimchi combos) do not apply. Units sold count "
"normally towards \"first sold\" milestones."
msgstr ""
"隔离：体育场的需求永远不会翻面为炸鸡，也永远不会搬走。它不能成为营销活动的目"
"标，替代效果（面条或寿司替换、泡菜组合）也不适用。售出的份数正常计入「首个卖"
"出」里程碑。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:145
msgid ""
"Milestone \"First stadium supplier\": The first player to win a stadium game "
"gains this Milestone. Reward: future announcements reach this player 3 turns "
"before the game instead of 2 - privately, one turn before everyone else "
"learns."
msgstr ""
"里程碑「首个体育场供应商」：第一位赢得体育场比赛的玩家获得该里程碑。奖励：此"
"后的公告会提前 3 回合而非 2 回合送达该玩家——且为私下送达，比其他玩家早 1 回合"
"得知。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:150
msgid ""
"With the Coffee module: For the Stadium's game-day walk (including coffee "
"bought along the way), the two arena tiles count as a single building - "
"moving between them never counts as a tile crossing. The walk can lap the "
"entire ring road, so a stocked coffee shop next to either half's road can "
"sell. All other customers count the two tiles as normal map tiles."
msgstr ""
"与咖啡模组联动：体育场在比赛日的步行（含沿途买的咖啡）把这两个板块算作同一栋建"
"筑——在两个板块之间移动永远不算跨板块边界。步行可以绕外环路走完整圈，因此贴着任"
"意一半环路的有货咖啡店都能卖出。其他顾客仍把这两个板块按普通地图板块计距。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:154
msgid "Labor Market"
msgstr "劳动力市场"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:160
msgid ""
"Labor Market turns staffing from private engine-building into a shared "
"contest. Each company has one Temporary Worker whose value rises as rivals "
"use theirs; Headhunters turn idle talent on the Beach into both an "
"opportunity and a liability; and Union Organizers make the largest active "
"workforces pay for their scale. These pressures overlap: sending more people "
"to work protects valuable staff but risks attracting a union, while resting "
"them limits company size but exposes them to competitors. Temporary Workers "
"offer a third path by producing more actions without adding more workers."
msgstr ""
"劳动力市场把原本各自经营的员工体系变成一场共同参与的人才竞争。每家公司只有1名"
"临时工，而且会随着其他玩家使用临时工而变强；猎头让休假区里的成熟人才同时成为"
"机会与风险；工会组织者则让上班人数最多的公司为规模付出代价。这些压力彼此交"
"织：让更多员工上班可以保护人才，却可能招来工会；让员工休假可以控制公司规模，"
"却会把他们暴露给竞争对手；临时工则提供了以更少人数换取更多行动的第三条路。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:161
#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:234
msgid "Rules"
msgstr "规则"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:163
msgid ""
"Temporary Worker: Every player starts with one on their Beach. At the start "
"of each turn, its action limit is frozen at 1 plus the number of Temporary "
"Workers removed before that turn. Before hiring, assign each action to "
"Waitress, Pricing Manager, Recruiting Girl, Trainer, Errand Boy, Marketing "
"Trainee or Kitchen Trainee. Different actions may copy different employees, "
"and the same employee may be chosen repeatedly. It is never doubled by Night "
"Shift, earns no salary and is permanently removed after that player's "
"Working Day. Unassigned or unused actions are forfeited."
msgstr ""
"临时工：每名玩家开局时在休假区获得1张。每回合开始时，其行动上限冻结为1加该回"
"合开始前已移除的临时工数。招聘前，为每次行动分别选择女服务员、定价经理、招聘"
"专员、培训师、跑腿伙计、营销实习生或厨房实习生；可混选不同员工，也可重复选择"
"同一员工。临时工不受夜班经理翻倍、不领工资，并在该玩家工作日后永久移除；未分"
"配或未使用的行动视为放弃。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:164
msgid ""
"Temporary Worker example: Two Temporary Workers had been removed before the "
"current turn, so every Temporary Worker used this turn receives 3 actions. "
"You may choose Trainer, Trainer and Recruiting Girl for two training actions "
"and one recruiting action. A rival using theirs later in the same turn also "
"receives 3 actions, even after yours has been removed."
msgstr ""
"临时工示例：本回合开始前已有2名临时工被移除，因此本回合使用的每名临时工都获得"
"3次行动。你可以选择培训师、培训师和招聘专员，从而获得2次培训行动和1次招聘行"
"动。即使你的临时工先被移除，同回合稍后使用临时工的对手也仍然只有相同的3次行"
"动。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:165
msgid ""
"Temporary campaigns: A Temporary Worker acting as a Marketing Trainee "
"creates a normal campaign, but no employee card is attached and nothing "
"returns to the Beach when it expires."
msgstr ""
"临时广告：临时工模仿营销实习生时建立正常广告，但不会有员工卡附着其上，广告到"
"期后也不会有员工返回休假区。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:166
msgid ""
"Headhunter: Train one level from a Management Trainee. It is a level-2 "
"salaried employee. Each working Headhunter may take one legal employee from "
"another player's current Beach. If that employee is still employed at "
"Payday, pay its normal salary, if any, plus a one-time job-switch salary of "
"$10 per employee level to the bank. If it is fired before Payday, no job-"
"switch salary is due. Temporary Workers, Headhunters, Union Organizers and "
"other non-transferable employees are illegal targets."
msgstr ""
"猎头：由管理培训生培训1级获得，是需要支付工资的2级员工。每名上班的猎头可从另"
"一名玩家当前休假区取得1名合法员工。若该员工在发薪时仍未被解雇，除其正常工资"
"（如有）外，还须向银行一次性支付员工等级乘$10的跳槽薪水；若发薪前解雇，则不支"
"付跳槽薪水。临时工、猎头、工会组织者和其他不可转移员工不能成为目标。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:167
msgid ""
"Headhunter example: You take a level-4 Senior Vice President from an "
"opponent's Beach. If you keep it until Payday, you pay its normal $5 salary "
"plus a one-time $40 job-switch salary to the bank, for $45 total. If you "
"fire it before Payday, neither payment is due for that employee."
msgstr ""
"猎头示例：你从对手的休假区挖走一名4级高级副总裁。若将其保留到发薪阶段，需要支"
"付正常的$5工资，并向银行额外支付一次性$40跳槽薪水，合计$45；若在发薪前将其解"
"雇，则不必为该员工支付这两项费用。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:168
msgid ""
"Unique employees and salary milestones: A Headhunter cannot take a unique "
"employee when the hiring player already owns the same unique employee. The "
"Headhunter action does not require cash on hand. The First to train someone "
"milestone reduces the combined normal and job-switch salaries by $15. The "
"First Trainer Used milestone protects all employees when the company still "
"cannot pay, following the normal bankruptcy rule. A job-switch salary is "
"removed after that Payday and is never charged again."
msgstr ""
"唯一员工与工资里程碑：如果猎头玩家已拥有同名唯一员工，则不能再挖走该员工；执"
"行猎头行动时无需持有足够现金。首个培训员工里程碑会从正常工资与跳槽薪水的合计"
"金额中减免$15。若公司仍无法支付，首个使用培训师里程碑按原破产规则保护全部员"
"工。跳槽薪水在本次发薪结算后移除，之后不再支付。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:169
msgid ""
"Union Organizer: The game uses one card per player, with inactive cards in "
"the public supply. After all Working Days, ignore companies with fewer than "
"5 workers, then give one Organizer to every company tied for the largest "
"eligible workforce. All other Organizer cards return to the public supply."
msgstr ""
"工会组织者：每名玩家对应1张卡，未生效的卡留在公共供应区。所有玩家工作日结束"
"后，先排除少于5名上班员工的公司，再给所有并列最大的合格公司各1张。其他工会组"
"织者返回公共供应区。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:170
msgid ""
"Union Organizer example: Companies A, B and C send 6, 6 and 5 employees to "
"work. All three meet the 5-worker threshold, but only A and B are tied for "
"the largest workforce, so each receives an Organizer for the next Working "
"Day; C receives none."
msgstr ""
"工会组织者示例：A、B、C公司本轮分别安排6名、6名和5名员工上班。三家公司都达到5"
"人门槛，但只有A和B并列上班人数最多，因此下一工作日A、B各获得1名工会组织者，C"
"不获得。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:171
msgid ""
"Each Union Organizer must occupy one slot directly under the CEO on the next "
"Working Day, provides no action or subordinate slots, and costs $5 at "
"Payday. It cannot be hired, trained, fired or headhunted, and it is excluded "
"from workforce counts. A working Temporary Worker counts as one employee "
"regardless of its number of actions."
msgstr ""
"每名工会组织者在下一工作日必须占用CEO下方的1个直属槽位，不提供行动或下属槽"
"位，并在发薪时支付$5。它不能招聘、培训、解雇或被猎头挖走，且不计入员工规模。"
"无论临时工执行多少次行动，上班时都只计1名员工。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:177
msgid "Second Bailout"
msgstr "二次救助"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:186
msgid ""
"In the base game the bank only breaks once. With this module the city steps "
"in the second time: the bank gets a fresh cash injection and every player "
"receives a free level-2 marketing employee. The game only ends for good on "
"the third break."
msgstr ""
"在基础游戏中，银行只会破产一次。启用本模组后，第二次破产时城市会出手相助：银"
"行获得一笔新的注资，每位玩家获得一名免费的 2 级营销员工。游戏要到第三次破产才"
"会真正结束。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:194
msgid ""
"First break: unchanged - reserve cards are cashed in (or prices re-picked "
"with the price-changing reserve cards) exactly as in the base game."
msgstr ""
"第一次破产：不变——储备卡按基础游戏的规则兑现（或使用改价储备卡重新定价）。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:199
msgid ""
"Second break: the city bails the bank out. The bank immediately receives "
"$300 per player (e.g. +$600 in a 2-player game, +$1500 with 5 players)."
msgstr ""
"第二次破产：城市出手救助银行。银行立即获得每名玩家 $300 的注资（例如 2 人局 +"
"$600，5 人局 +$1500）。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:204
msgid ""
"The gift: on the night of the bailout, players pick one free level-2 "
"marketing employee each, in turn order, first come first served: Campaign "
"Manager (always), plus Rural Marketeer, Mass Marketeer, Gourmet Food Critic "
"or Hawker Marketeer if the matching module is enabled in this game. A card "
"that is sold out in the talent market cannot be picked; if nothing is left "
"when your turn comes, you get nothing. You may also decline."
msgstr ""
"赠礼：在获得救助的当晚，玩家按回合顺序各挑选一名免费的 2 级营销员工，先到先"
"得：营销经理（始终可选），若本局启用了相应模组，还可选乡村推销员、大众推销"
"员、美食评论家或小贩营销员。人才市场中已售罄的卡不能选；轮到你时若已无剩余，"
"则一无所获。你也可以放弃。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:209
msgid ""
"The gift is not a hire: it does not trigger \"first to hire 3 employees\" "
"style milestones. The employee joins your beach and is paid like any other "
"employee - getting them onto the schedule and affording their salary is your "
"problem. Module milestones (e.g. \"first Rural Marketeer used\") still "
"trigger normally the first time you market with them."
msgstr ""
"赠礼不算招聘：它不会触发「首个雇佣 3 名员工」之类的里程碑。该员工会加入你的休"
"假区，并像其他员工一样支付工资——把他安排进组织结构并付得起工资，是你自己的问"
"题。模组里程碑（例如「首个使用乡村推销员」）仍会在你第一次用他进行营销时正常"
"触发。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:214
msgid "Third break: the game ends immediately - there is only one bailout."
msgstr "第三次破产：游戏立即结束——救助只有一次。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:219
msgid ""
"Short games are unaffected: the first break already ends them, so the "
"bailout never happens."
msgstr "短局不受影响：第一次破产就已结束游戏，因此救助永远不会发生。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:228
msgid "Media Line"
msgstr "传媒线"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:229
msgid "Telemarketer"
msgstr "电话营销员"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:230
msgid "TV Announcer"
msgstr "电视播音员"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:233
msgid ""
"The base game's marketing is paper: billboards, mail, airplanes. This module "
"adds the airwaves. A Telemarketer calls the houses right next door - no "
"roads required, one call per house. A TV Announcer mounts antennas on five "
"nearby roofs and owns the news: one story moves every price in the city by "
"$5 tomorrow, up or down. Demand is small but surgical - the payoff is one "
"perfectly stocked jackpot night that can break the bank."
msgstr ""
"基础游戏的营销靠纸面：广告牌、邮件、飞机。本模组则加入了电波。电话营销员直接"
"致电紧邻的房屋——无需道路，每栋房屋一通电话。电视播音员在附近五栋房屋的屋顶架"
"设天线，掌控新闻：一则报道会让明天全城的所有价格上下浮动 $5。需求虽小却精准——"
"回报是完美备货的头奖之夜，足以让银行破产。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:236
msgid ""
"Training chain: Marketing Trainee → Telemarketer (level 2) → TV Announcer "
"(level 3) → Brand Director. Six of each; cards may be stacked."
msgstr ""
"培训链：营销实习生 → 电话营销员（2 级）→ 电视播音员（3 级）→ 品牌总监。每种"
"各 6 张；可叠放。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:237
msgid ""
"Telemarketer: places 2x1 phone tokens attached to buildings (not roads) "
"within one orthogonal step of your restaurant (a cross of 5 tiles). Each "
"action places up to two tokens - two calls with the same food and duration, "
"placed together; you may place only one. A token wedged between two houses "
"reaches both. Duration 1-3 nights. The city has only 6 tokens: at most 6 "
"calls on the board at once."
msgstr ""
"电话营销员：在你的餐厅正交方向一格范围内（5 个板块组成的十字）放置 2x1 的电话"
"标记，须附着在建筑（而非道路）上。每次行动最多放置两个标记——两通电话的食物和"
"时长相同，一起放置；也可以只放一个。夹在两栋房屋之间的标记可同时覆盖两者。时"
"长 1-3 回合。全城只有 6 个标记：版面上最多同时存在 6 通电话。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:238
msgid ""
"TV Announcer: picks exactly 5 houses within 2 steps of your restaurant (a "
"diamond of 13 tiles) and mounts a rooftop antenna on each. Duration 1-4 "
"nights. The city has only 2 channels: at most 2 TV campaigns at once; one "
"player holding both has a monopoly."
msgstr ""
"电视播音员：在你的餐厅 2 格范围内（13 个板块组成的菱形）恰好选择 5 栋房屋，并"
"在每栋屋顶架设天线。时长 1-4 回合。全城只有 2 个频道：最多同时存在 2 个电视营"
"销活动；若一名玩家同时持有两个，则形成垄断。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:239
msgid ""
"Headline (TV Announcer only, free, one per working announcer per turn): "
"tomorrow night every sale in the city pays +$5 (Prime Time) or -$5 (Bad "
"Press). Stories stack and cancel each other out, clamped to a city-wide "
"total of +$10 or -$10."
msgstr ""
"头条（仅限电视播音员，免费，每名在岗播音员每回合一次）：明天晚上，全城的每笔"
"销售 +$5（黄金时段）或 -$5（负面报道）。报道会叠加并互相抵消，全城总计上限为 "
"+$10 或 -$10。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:240
msgid ""
"Timing: campaigns start pushing demand the turn after placement, like all "
"campaigns. Houses keep the usual 3-demand cap; the different media push in a "
"fixed order."
msgstr ""
"时机：与其他所有营销活动一样，营销活动在放置后的下一回合开始推动需求。房屋保"
"持平常的 3 点需求上限；不同媒介按固定顺序推动。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:241
msgid "Unserved orders stay on the house and may be fulfilled by anyone."
msgstr "未被满足的订单会留在房屋上，任何人都可以供货。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:242
msgid ""
"Milestone \"First Telemarketer used\": unlocks a permanent group bonus - at "
"Dinnertime, if every house of one of your media groups (the 2 phone houses "
"or the 5 antenna houses) is served entirely by you, earn $10 per house ($20 "
"per phone group, $50 per TV group; groups settle separately). Requires "
"purity: no other marketing employees or campaigns of yours may be active "
"that night."
msgstr ""
"里程碑「首个使用电话营销员」：解锁一项永久团队奖励——晚餐结算时，若你某个媒体"
"组（2 栋电话房屋或 5 栋天线房屋）的每栋房屋都由你独家供应，则每栋房屋获得 $10"
"（电话组 $20，电视组 $50；各组单独结算）。要求纯粹性：当晚不得有其他由你发起"
"的营销员工或营销活动处于活跃状态。"

#: .\FCM\templates\FCM\fanExpansionsHelp.html:243
msgid ""
"Milestone \"First TV Announcer used\": one-time launch bonus - during your "
"first TV campaign, every antenna house gets 2 demand per night instead of 1."
msgstr ""
"里程碑「首个使用电视播音员」：一次性首播奖励——在你的第一个电视营销活动期间，"
"每栋天线房屋每晚获得 2 点需求而非 1 点。"

